 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "94:1-7 carries Al-Muyassar's purpose of the verse («إقامة الحجة على المشركين بشهادة أهل الكتاب»), so the conditional addressed to the Prophet ﷺ is not misread. 94-95 address him: no plate. No plate on Yunus's name (98:9). Al-Muyassar's «توبة نصوحا» (66:8) is cut before. STAGING v4: c1 (94-95) stays ambient: it is addressed to the Prophet ﷺ himself (a conditional and a warning about his own certainty), so nothing is staged, no one is shown reading the Scripture and no plate is used; mood changed from light to night_sky (95 is a warning: light is never the mood over a threat), and params.quiet turns off the word pulses over all of 94-95. c2 (96-97): those on whom the word of the Lord came into effect: three faceless men in dark robes in a town by day; the camera on them (96:3, 97:5); a seal plate for the word of your Lord (96:5-8); no gesture inside the negated 96:7-8 or the conditional 97:1-4; nothing of the punishment is drawn (97:5-8). c3 (98): the people of Yunus, a town that believed and was spared: a town by day, its people three faceless men (the series' sign for a group, no number meant; no woman in a story scene; not the uncountable crowd whose rocks read as idols). 98:1-6 (no other town benefited from a late faith) is held wide. Yunus himself is not drawn: the verse names him only to identify his people, and neither tafsir places him among them when they believed; the camera is wide when he is named (98:9). They lower their heads (98:10) and raise their hands (98:11) as they believe and repent (Al-Muyassar: they repented to Allah when they were sure the punishment was coming); no plate is on screen while their hands are raised. The punishment that was lifted is never drawn (no cloud, storm or darkness); the camera on them for We removed from them (98:13); an hourglass for We gave them enjoyment for a time (98:19-21)."
 },
